<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Content changes and scrolls are what move text under the overlay, so those are the
  events worth waking for; window state changes tell us the foreground app switched.
  The service reads window content (that is the whole point) and asks for the extra
  per-character bounds it needs to place a transcription on one word rather than on a
  whole paragraph.

  Views the app marks unimportant for accessibility are deliberately not requested. Every
  node in the tree is a round trip into that app, and those round trips are almost all of
  the latency; the decorative containers that flag pulls in carry no text worth reading.

  The accessibility button is deliberately not requested. A service that asks for it is
  presented as a shortcut rather than as a service: its page in Settings then offers only
  "shortcut, off" and no switch to turn the service on at all, which leaves it unusable on a
  phone where that shortcut has not been set up. The shade tile is the trigger instead, and a
  reader who wants the button can bind it from the same page.

  Windows changing is asked for so that the button can stand clear of a keyboard: a keyboard
  is a window of its own, and it opening or closing is announced as nothing else. It costs a
  cheap look at where the button belongs, not a read of the screen.

  notificationTimeout is zero rather than the usual 100ms: it is how often the system is
  allowed to hand us anything at all, and at 100ms a fling delivered one or two events in
  its whole length, so the transcriptions were re-read twice during a movement of two
  thousand pixels.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowContentChanged|typeViewScrolled|typeWindowStateChanged|typeWindowsChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault|flagReportViewIds|flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:canTakeScreenshot="true"
    android:description="@string/service_description"
    android:notificationTimeout="0"
    android:settingsActivity="io.github.nanbiz.phonetix.MainActivity" />
